## Why This Is Asked
Tests augmented BST design for duplicates and range queries on a dynamic multiset, focusing on balance, memory, and correctness.

## Key Concepts
- Treap with duplicates via per-node cnt
- Subtree size and sum augmentation
- kth smallest by counts; range queries via splits or traversal

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node{constructor(key,prio){this.key=key;this.prio=prio;this.cnt=1;this.l=null;this.r=null;this.sz=1;this.sum=key}};
function upd(n){if(!n)return; n.sz=n.cnt+(n.l?.sz||0)+(n.r?.sz||0); n.sum=n.key*n.cnt+(n.l?.sum||0)+(n.r?.sum||0)}
function rotateRight(y){const x=y.l; y.l=x.r; x.r=y; upd(y); upd(x); return x}
function rotateLeft(x){const y=x.r; x.r=y.l; y.l=x; upd(x); upd(y); return y}
function insert(n, key){if(!n)return new Node(key,Math.random()); if(key===n.key){n.cnt++; upd(n);return n}; if(key<n.key){n.l=insert(n.l,key); if(n.l.prio>n.prio) n=rotateRight(n);} else {n.r=insert(n.r,key); if(n.r.prio>n.prio) n=rotateLeft(n);} upd(n); return n}
function kth(n,k){if(!n) return null; const leftSize=n.l?.sz||0; if(k<=leftSize) return kth(n.l,k); if(k>leftSize+n.cnt) return kth(n.r,k-leftSize-n.cnt); return n.key;}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of adaptive prefix data structures and space-time trade-offs for dynamic multisets with non-trivial sum queries.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node aggregates; handling duplicates; update of subtree sums on insert/delete; edge cases when counts drop to zero.

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.endCount = 0;
    this.subLen = 0;
  }
}
class WordTrie {
  constructor(){ this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word){ let node=this.root; for(const ch of word){ node.subLen += word.length; if(!node.children.has(ch)) node.children.set(ch,new TrieNode()); node = node.children.get(ch); } node.subLen += word.length; node.endCount += 1; }
  delete(word){ let node=this.root; for(const ch of word){ if(!node.children.has(ch)) return; node.subLen -= word.length; node = node.children.get(ch); } node.subLen -= word.length; if(node.endCount>0) node.endCount -= 1; }
  query(prefix){ let node=this.root; for(const ch of prefix){ if(!node.children.has(ch)) return 0; node = node.children.get(ch); } return node.subLen; }
}
```

